From: j7 battery
Subject: a5xelte: let the SweetBattery personality match on this board

0336 added an S2MU004 fuel-gauge driver and compiled SweetBattery for A5XELTE, but the personality
itself sits behind `#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE) || defined(...HEROLTE)` in
iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp, so nothing ever matched the class and the probe never ran: the boot
log has no "SWEET BATTERY:" line at all and powerd keeps its 1 % fallback.  AppleCLCD keeps its own
A5XELTE guard because this board presents through SweetFB.

diff --git a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
index b89b64d..e07d3ae 100644
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -89,7 +89,12 @@ const char * gIOKernelConfigTables =
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOResources;"
     "     'IOMatchCategory' = SweetHIDTouch;"
     "   },"
-#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_HEROLTE)
+/* 0337: this used to read `!defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE) || defined(...HEROLTE)`,
+ * which is why the J7 Prime showed powerd's 1 % icon: SweetBattery was compiled and linked
+ * but no personality ever matched it, so neither "SWEET BATTERY:" nor the fuel-gauge probe
+ * ran.  AppleCLCD above keeps its own A5XELTE guard because this board presents through
+ * SweetFB instead. */
+#if 1                                                   /* every board, A5XELTE included */
     "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = SweetBattery;"
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOResources;"
